verses.commentary:
25:2 The names in v. 2 are well established Arab tribes. The most noted is Midian (cf. Gen. 36:35;
37:28; Exod. 2:15,16; 3:1; 18:1; Num. 25:15; 31:3,8,9; Judges 6-8; see note at Exod. 2:15). An excellent
graph of these Arabian tribes can be found in Leupold's commentary on Genesis, vol. 2, p. 690.

25:13 "Kedar" This is the most predominate tribe of Ishmael (BDB 871, cf. Isa. 21:16-17; 42:11;
Jer. 2:10; 49:28; Ps. 120:5). The tribes of Ishmael were located to the east and the south of the tribes
of Keturah's sons.
